-- title:
--   Minimal primes of varpi in a stalk read on an affine chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings with $S$ an $R$-algebra, let $X$ be a scheme, let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism, and let $\iota : \operatorname{Spec} S \to X$ be an open immersion such that $\iota$ followed by $f$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to S$. Fix $\varpi \in R$ and a point $q$ of $\operatorname{Spec} S$, i.e. a prime ideal $q^{\mathrm{as}} =$ `q.asIdeal` of $S$. Write $t \in \mathcal{O}_{X,\iota(q)}$ for the germ at $\iota(q)$ of the global section $f^{\#}(\varpi)$ of $X$, obtained by transporting $\varpi$ into $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R)$ through the inverse of the canonical isomorphism $R \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R)$, pulling back along $f$ on global sections, and taking the germ at $\iota(q)$. The assertion is an equivalence: the set of minimal primes of the principal ideal $(t)$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\iota(q)}$ fails to be a subsingleton — that is, it contains two distinct elements — if and only if there exist prime ideals $\mathfrak{p} \neq \mathfrak{p}'$ of $S$, both minimal over the principal ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $S$, with $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq q^{\mathrm{as}}$ and $\mathfrak{p}' \subseteq q^{\mathrm{as}}$.
--
--   This is the dictionary that converts a statement about the branching of the divisor of $\varpi$ at a point of a scheme $X$ into a statement about minimal primes of $\varpi S$ in an affine chart $\operatorname{Spec} S \subseteq X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$. It is used in the analysis of the special fibre of integral models of the modular curves $X_1(p)$, where the charts are given by explicit coordinate rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_not_subsingleton_minimalPrimes_span_germ_iff_exists_two_minimalPrimes_le_of_chart.lean

